author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Both SDK and CLI gates bracket their measurements with warmed bare-process controls and portable environment evidence; over-budget or missing controls fail with product admission unverified and retain the full report; qualified product regressions still fail and retain all violations; positive and negative controls pass without any product budget increase; public methodology and linked evidence document the historical diagnosis boundary.
value: Context management needs trustworthy performance evidence that separates observed runner qualification from product admission.
parent: pm-bj7rq0
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: SDK and CLI startup gates now retain warmed controls before and after the measured census plus portable runner observations. Missing or over-budget controls reject product admission as unverified; qualified product regressions retain all violations and fail unchanged latency and RSS budgets.
expected_result: "Runner qualification and product admission are independently explicit; failed or missing controls never certify product success, and real product regressions remain unsuccessful."
actual_result: "All 27 linked benchmark tests passed. Both real startup gates passed on CI Node24 with unchanged ceilings. Node26 unqualified controls and a separate qualified merge overrun remain recorded, and the parent historical-cause diagnosis remains open. Full local suite passed before the later pure argv extraction; 144 focused tests and typecheck passed afterward."
